From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: xiaomi-n1: match stock command transfer parameters

The N1 60 Hz stock timing selects 1.36 GHz DSI lanes, a 7300 us MDP
transfer budget and two DSC slices per packet. The initial driver copied
its porches but did not account for the separate downstream lane clock,
so MSM selected about 677 MHz and sent each slice in a separate packet.

Express the command transfer overhead in the horizontal blanking used
by MSM's clock calculation and select the existing all-slices packet
flag. Keep the panel refresh at 60 Hz, its vertical TE timing, DSC PPS,
initialization sequence and brightness controls unchanged.

This follows the command-mode porch approach described by Abhinav Kumar
and used by Marijn Suijten's SOFEF01 proposal, with a local derivation for
N1's DSC 10bpc/8bpp mode rather than copying the non-DSC panel timings:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2306.1/05026.html
https://www.mail-archive.com/dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org/msg581526.html

The packet flag is already supported by the selected kernel and is also
used by the Sheng panel. No DSI host API or shared clock policy changes.
This corrects transport configuration mismatches; intermittent physical
snow still requires visual acceptance, not merely a clean screenshot.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-xiaomi-n1.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-xiaomi-n1.c
@@ -252,9 +252,23 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The stock 60 Hz mode uses a 1.36 GHz lane rate and a 7300 us MDP
+ * transfer budget. Copying its video-style porches gives only 677 MHz
+ * with MSM's DSC clock calculation, extending the payload to 13.6 ms.
+ *
+ * Command mode has no wire-level horizontal porches. Represent the
+ * transfer budget in horizontal blanking, as required by the current MSM
+ * host, while retaining 60 Hz and the original vertical/TE timing:
+ *   compressed active = ceil(1440 * 8 / 30) = 384
+ *   compressed total = ceil(1360000000 * 4 / (30 * 3244 * 60)) = 932
+ *   htotal = 1440 + (932 - 384) = 1988
+ * The resulting lane rate is 1.36053 GHz (within 0.04% of stock).
+ * See dsi_adjust_pclk_for_compression(); this does not change DDIC commands.
+ */
 static const struct drm_display_mode n1_mode = {
-	.clock = 295853,
-	.hdisplay = 1440, .hsync_start = 1472, .hsync_end = 1488, .htotal = 1520,
+	.clock = 386944,
+	.hdisplay = 1440, .hsync_start = 1472, .hsync_end = 1488, .htotal = 1988,
 	.vdisplay = 3200, .vsync_start = 3216, .vsync_end = 3220, .vtotal = 3244,
 	.width_mm = 70, .height_mm = 156,
 	.type = DRM_MODE_TYPE_DRIVER | DRM_MODE_TYPE_PREFERRED,
@@ -317,7 +331,9 @@
 		return PTR_ERR(ctx->panel.backlight);
 	dsi->lanes = 4;
 	dsi->format = MIPI_DSI_FMT_RGB101010;
-	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS;
+	/* Stock qcom,mdss-dsc-slice-per-pkt = <2>: one full line per packet. */
+	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS |
+			  MIPI_DSI_MODE_DSC_ALL_SLICES_IN_PKT;
 	ctx->dsc = (struct drm_dsc_config) {
 		.dsc_version_major = 1, .dsc_version_minor = 2,
 		.slice_height = 20, .slice_width = 720, .slice_count = 2,
